## AI Fix Checklist — Logging

**Invocation:** When the user says **"fix logging"**, **"fix logger"**, **"logging compliance"**, or **"apply logging rules"**, use this checklist to audit and fix code.

### Main app (`src/`)

- [ ] No `console.log`, `console.error`, `console.warn`, `console.info`, `console.debug` — use `const log = MainAppLogger.instance` (from `@ocentra/logging-domain/core/mainAppLogger`) or equivalent.
- [ ] All log calls use `getStackTrace()` as second argument (from `@ocentra/logging-domain/core/stackTrace`).
- [ ] Imports from `@ocentra/logging-domain` (not ad-hoc loggers). Init via `initLogging()` from `@/lib/logging/init` at app bootstrap.
- [ ] Module-level flags (`LOG_DECK`, etc.) are used correctly (last arg `enabled` for conditional logs).
- [ ] If adding build-time stripping: use `__LOGGING_ENABLED__` or `__DEV__` around verbose log blocks.

### Cloudflare (`infra/cloudflare/`)

- [ ] Handler/DO/test uses `Logger`, `getStackTrace`, `flushAllBatchesAndTestLogs` from `@/logging/domain-logger-init`.
- [ ] `log.register(import.meta.url)` and helpers `logInfo`, `logWarn`, `logError`, `logDebug` present.
- [ ] Every `logInfo`/`logWarn`/`logError`/`logDebug` call passes `getStackTrace()` as second argument.
- [ ] `afterEach` / `afterAll` calls `flushAllBatchesAndTestLogs()` where required by test setup.
- [ ] No raw `console.*` for application logging — use domain logger.

### General

- [ ] No mock or fake logger that bypasses `@ocentra/logging-domain` for money-critical or security paths.
- [ ] See `ocentra-cloudflare-logging.mdc` for exact pattern in new handlers/DOs/tests.

